#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"
PREVIOUS PROMPT 1:

In 02-exodus/ chapters 28-40, only in the P sections, when P's getting really excited about his clothes and the tabernacle and Aaron becoming the high priest, add some English with Niqqud to show P getting all worked up.

Give English niqqud to these words every time they appear in P in that range.

gold, golden, blue, purple, scarlet, linen, onyx, Aaron, ephod, holy, holies, Holy, Holiness, breastplate, judgment, carnelian, topaz, emerald, ruby, sapphire, diamond, jacinth, agate, amethyst, beryl, onyx, jasper, belt, rings, Urim, Tummim, pomegranates, bell, headdress, sash, Tent of Meeting, incense, cubit, shekel, anointing, glory, beauty

Keep the niqqud consistent, they should be the correct niqqud for the vowels of the word in question.

Then write a file at the end saying how many times each word appeared in each chapter, and overall in the section, and overall in all of P in [01][0-9]-*/*.tex.

Only add the english niqqud to Exodus 28 to Exodus 40, and only in P.

Go!

PREVIOUS PROMPT 2:

Ok great work so far, but I want much more intense niqqud on each word. As a second attempt, let's add not just the niqqud like we already have, we need more.

So now:

Remember you can put english niqqud on more than just vowels! Also add them on ds an ts to the right or wherever you think they fit, because the hebrew does. (Dagesh or whatever I forget the name, just add as many dots as you can possibly justify.)

Also remember you can add cantillation marks too! We want to make P practically be screaming as he gets more excited.

That said, try to avoid putting niqqud that appear UNDER a letter in a place that will cause it to overlap with the tail of a letter that extends lower like p or g, and try to avoid putting upper niqqud on capital letters or letters with bits protruding upward, like d or b.

Do that now, and work until you're satisfied.


PREVIOUS PROMPT 3:
Remove the dagesh's from the consonants and any dots that go horizontally between letters.
Remove the 3 underdots from the p in ephod.
Remove the final niqqud or cantillation from the words like headdress and breastplate and linen: it's two vertical dots like a colon up high and it's trailing over to the next word.
In scarlett, there are 3 diagonal down cantillations, remove the first, it's interfering with the : shaped thing above the c.
In onyx, you can keep the horizontal dot between the y and x, it's a good dagesh type thing and not too overlappy.
Remove the upper dots that are showing up at the top left of lowercase "l"s, they're colliding with the l.
The little hollow circle above the d in judgement is colliding, move it elsewhere, on a letter that's not higher than an ascii x.
In purple, remove the diagonal up to the right cantillation between the r and p, it's overlapping some other mark.
The r in scarlett has two marks under it, choose one.
Remove the diamond above the d in emerald.
The word agate should have no marks below the g, they're colliding.
Do anything else like the above that I didn't mention.

CURRENT PROMPT:
Nevermind, just add an absurd and ridiculous numbers of niqqud (no cantillation) to all the words in the first prompt wherever they appear in Exodus 28-40. Avoid the bottoms of lower letter stems like p and g, avoid the tops of uppers like d and b and capitals, but go nuts, put niqqud on consontants and vowels of these words, in whatever arrangement most highlights P's giant boner of excitement at the idea that everyone has to bring him gold and make him pretty clothes.
EOF
